---
---

<section
  id="capabilities"
  class="py-12 sm:py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-7xl mx-auto border-t-2 border-ink/15"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight uppercase leading-none">
      What OmniBuf does{' '}
      <span class="font-serif italic font-normal normal-case text-[#FF4F18]">beyond Protobuf.</span>
    </h2>
  </div>

  <div class="border-t-2 border-ink divide-y-2 divide-ink/20">
    <!-- Row 1: Schema-Less Wire Inspection -->
    <div class="py-8 sm:py-10 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 space-y-2.5 min-w-0">
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Every wire type is explicit
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[65ch]">
          In Protobuf, strings, byte slices, sub-messages, maps, and packed arrays all share{' '}
          <code>Wire Type 2</code>, while 32-bit and 64-bit wire types mix floats with signed and
          unsigned fixed integers. OmniBuf's 4-bit tag and explicit collection headers give each of
          those its own wire type so <code>DecodeBlind</code> recovers the exact wire type and value
          of every present field without a schema (while enum label names, omitted defaults, and
          inactive <code>oneof</code> fields still require a schema).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3.5 font-mono text-sm min-w-0">
        <div class="p-4 bg-[#FAF8F2] border-2 border-ink rounded-md overflow-x-auto">
          <!-- prettier-ignore -->
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-ink/75 mb-1.5">
            <a href="https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protoscope" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="doc-link">protoscope</a>
          </div>
          <pre class="text-sm text-ink/85 leading-snug"><span class="text-[#C23000] font-bold">3:</span> 1 <span class="text-ink/75"># int or bool?</span>
<span class="text-[#C23000] font-bold">9:</span> &#123;<span class="text-ink/75">"\x1a\x03FRA\x20*"</span>&#125;</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-ink text-paper border-2 border-ink rounded-md overflow-x-auto">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-acid mb-1.5">omnibuf decode</div>
          <pre class="text-sm text-paper/95 leading-snug">&#123;<span class="text-acid font-bold">"3":</span> <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">true</span>,
 <span class="text-acid font-bold">"9":</span> &#123;<span class="text-acid">"3":</span> <span class="text-paper font-bold">"FRA"</span>, <span class="text-acid">"4":</span> 42&#125;&#125;</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Row 2: Optional Field #0 Inline Field Names -->
    <div class="py-8 sm:py-10 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 space-y-2.5 min-w-0">
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Optional inline field names (written once in Field #0)
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[65ch]">
          By default, packets only carry field numbers to stay small. If you want string keys on the
          wire too, turn on <code>Field #0</code> (<code>omnibuf.v1.SchemaMeta</code>). That writes
          the field-name table once at the top of the packet, and for arrays or maps of nested
          messages it records the child field names only once on the parent field instead of
          repeating key strings inside every item like JSON or MessagePack. Even with Field #0
          enabled, our 11-field test packet (with 4 nested <code>Neighbor</code> messages) is{' '}
          <code>630 B</code>, which is smaller than both MessagePack (<code>656 B</code>) and JSON (
          <code>803 B</code>).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 font-mono text-sm min-w-0">
        <div class="p-4 bg-ink text-paper border-2 border-ink rounded-md overflow-x-auto">
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-acid mb-1.5">
            omnibuf decode (packet with Field #0)
          </div>
          <pre class="text-sm text-paper/95 leading-snug">&#123;<span class="text-acid font-bold">"active":</span> <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">true</span>,
 <span class="text-acid font-bold">"location":</span> &#123;<span class="text-acid">"city":</span> <span class="text-paper font-bold">"FRA"</span>, <span class="text-acid">"rack":</span> 42&#125;&#125;</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Row 3: Raw Concatenation Merge -->
    <div class="py-8 sm:py-10 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 lg:gap-8 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 space-y-2.5 min-w-0">
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Merge messages by appending raw bytes
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[65ch]">
          Packets have no file header or footer. Later scalar fields overwrite earlier ones, and
          repeated fields append. If you concatenate two encoded buffers (
          <code>append(msgA, msgB...)</code>), the result is already a valid merged message. No
          decode or re-encode step required.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 font-mono text-sm min-w-0">
        <div class="p-4 bg-ink text-paper border-2 border-ink rounded-md overflow-x-auto">
          <pre class="text-sm text-paper/95 leading-relaxed"><span class="text-paper/65">msgA:</span> &#123;<span class="text-acid">"id":</span> 1, <span class="text-acid">"active":</span> <span class="text-paper/70">false</span>&#125;
<span class="text-paper/65">msgB:</span> &#123;<span class="text-acid">"active":</span> <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">true</span>&#125;

<span class="text-acid font-bold">append(msgA, msgB...)</span> &rarr; &#123;<span class="text-acid">"id":</span> 1, <span class="text-acid">"active":</span> <span class="text-[#FF4F18] font-bold">true</span>&#125;</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Row 4: Native Maps -->
    <div class="py-8 sm:py-10 space-y-6">
      <div class="space-y-3 min-w-0">
        <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-snug">
          Native map wire type
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[75ch]">
          Protobuf doesn't have a dedicated wire type for maps. When you write{' '}
          <code>map&lt;string, uint64&gt; counters = 1</code>, the compiler turns it into a repeated
          sub-message (<code>repeated CountersEntry</code>) behind the scenes. Every key-value pair
          gets wrapped in 4 extra bytes of field tags and sub-message lengths (<code>0a 05</code>,{' '}
          <code>0a</code>, <code>10</code>), and the decoder has to parse a sub-message for every
          entry in the map.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[75ch]">
          OmniBuf has a native map wire type (<code>WireMap = 14</code>). It writes a 2-byte header
          with the key and value wire types once (<code>0A 00</code> for{' '}
          <code>WireString = 10</code> and <code>WireUint = 0</code>), followed by the entry count
          and the raw <code>[Key][Value]</code> pairs. In this example, each entry takes{' '}
          <strong>3 bytes instead of 7</strong> (36 B vs. 70 B for a 10-entry map).
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Clean Map Lowering & Wire Hex Diagram -->
      <div class="os-window overflow-hidden">
        <div class="os-titlebar bg-[#E5E0D5]">
          <span class="font-mono text-sm sm:text-base font-bold uppercase">
            Map Lowering &amp; Wire Hex: Protobuf vs. OmniBuf
          </span>
          <div class="os-stripes"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white p-3 sm:p-6">
          <!-- DESKTOP SVG -->
          <div class="hidden md:block">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 900 332"
              class="w-full h-auto select-none"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Diagram showing map<string, uint64> counters = 1 schema and {'a': 1, 'b': 2} input joined together, then branching to Protobuf (which lowers into a synthetic CountersEntry sub-message before 14-byte wire hex) and OmniBuf (which skips Step 2 directly to 12-byte WireMap hex)."
            >
              <defs>
                <marker
                  id="map-arr-ink"
                  viewBox="0 0 10 10"
                  refX="7"
                  refY="5"
                  markerWidth="6"
                  markerHeight="6"
                  orient="auto"
                >
                  <polygon points="0,1 10,5 0,9" fill="context-stroke" />
                </marker>
              </defs>

              <!-- Column Headers -->
              <text
                x="16"
                y="24"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="12"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                1. SCHEMA &amp; INPUT
              </text>
              <text
                x="280"
                y="24"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="12"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                2. COMPILER LOWERING
              </text>
              <text
                x="584"
                y="24"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="12"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                3. WIRE PAYLOAD HEX
              </text>

              <!-- ============================================================ -->
              <!-- STEP 1: SEPARATE SCHEMA & INPUT BOXES                        -->
              <!-- ============================================================ -->
              <!-- Schema Box -->
              <rect
                x="16"
                y="64"
                width="196"
                height="92"
                rx="6"
                fill="#FAF8F2"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2"
              />
              <text
                x="30"
                y="104"
                fill="#C23000"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="13"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                map&lt;string, uint64&gt;
              </text>
              <text
                x="30"
                y="128"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="13.5"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                counters = 1;
              </text>

              <!-- Input Box -->
              <rect
                x="16"
                y="208"
                width="196"
                height="92"
                rx="6"
                fill="#FAF8F2"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2"
              />
              <text
                x="30"
                y="259"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="13.5"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                &#123;"a": 1, "b": 2&#125;
              </text>

              <!-- Join Schema & Input -> Single Trunk -> Branch to Protobuf & OmniBuf -->
              <path
                d="M 212 110 L 230 110 L 230 254 L 212 254"
                fill="none"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2.2"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
              <line x1="230" y1="182" x2="250" y2="182" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="2.2" />

              <!-- ============================================================ -->
              <!-- TOP TRACK: PROTOBUF (Step 1 -> Step 2 -> Step 3)             -->
              <!-- ============================================================ -->
              <text
                x="280"
                y="52"
                fill="#C23000"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="13"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                PROTOBUF
              </text>

              <!-- Branch from joined trunk -> Protobuf Step 2 -->
              <path
                d="M 250 182 L 250 110 L 274 110"
                fill="none"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2.2"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                marker-end="url(#map-arr-ink)"
              />

              <!-- Protobuf Step 2: Synthetic CountersEntry -->
              <rect
                x="280"
                y="64"
                width="268"
                height="92"
                rx="6"
                fill="#FAF8F2"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2"
              />
              <text
                x="294"
                y="90"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="11.5"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                message CountersEntry &#123;
              </text>
              <text x="306" y="110" fill="#111111" font-family="IBM Plex Mono" font-size="11.5">
                string key = 1; uint64 value = 2;
              </text>
              <text
                x="294"
                y="128"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="11.5"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                &#125;
              </text>
              <text
                x="294"
                y="146"
                fill="#C23000"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="11.5"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                repeated CountersEntry counters = 1;
              </text>

              <!-- Arrow: Protobuf Step 2 -> Protobuf Step 3 -->
              <line
                x1="548"
                y1="110"
                x2="578"
                y2="110"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2.2"
                marker-end="url(#map-arr-ink)"
              />

              <!-- Protobuf Step 3: Pure Wire Hex -->
              <rect
                x="584"
                y="64"
                width="300"
                height="92"
                rx="6"
                fill="#FAF8F2"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2"
              />
              <text
                x="600"
                y="101"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="15"
                font-weight="700"
                letter-spacing="0.5"
              >
                <tspan fill="#FF4F18">0A 05 0A</tspan> 01 61 <tspan fill="#FF4F18">10</tspan> 01
              </text>
              <text
                x="600"
                y="134"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="15"
                font-weight="700"
                letter-spacing="0.5"
              >
                <tspan fill="#FF4F18">0A 05 0A</tspan> 01 62 <tspan fill="#FF4F18">10</tspan> 02
              </text>
              <text
                x="884"
                y="174"
                fill="#C23000"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="12"
                font-weight="700"
                text-anchor="end"
              >
                14 bytes
              </text>

              <!-- ============================================================ -->
              <!-- BOTTOM TRACK: OMNIBUF (Branch skipping Step 2 -> Step 3)     -->
              <!-- ============================================================ -->
              <text
                x="280"
                y="240"
                fill="#111111"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="13"
                font-weight="700"
              >
                OMNIBUF
              </text>

              <!-- Branch from joined trunk straight across Step 2 to Step 3 -->
              <path
                d="M 250 182 L 250 254 L 578 254"
                fill="none"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2.2"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                marker-end="url(#map-arr-ink)"
              />

              <!-- OmniBuf Step 3: Pure Wire Hex -->
              <rect
                x="584"
                y="208"
                width="300"
                height="92"
                rx="6"
                fill="#111111"
                stroke="#111111"
                stroke-width="2"
              />
              <text
                x="600"
                y="236"
                fill="#D4FF33"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="15"
                font-weight="700"
                letter-spacing="0.5"
              >
                3D 26 00 0A 00 05
              </text>
              <text
                x="600"
                y="263"
                fill="#FAF8F2"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="15"
                font-weight="700"
                letter-spacing="0.5"
              >
                03 61 03
              </text>
              <text
                x="600"
                y="287"
                fill="#FAF8F2"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="15"
                font-weight="700"
                letter-spacing="0.5"
              >
                03 62 05
              </text>
              <text
                x="884"
                y="318"
                fill="#00805A"
                font-family="IBM Plex Mono"
                font-size="12"
                font-weight="700"
                text-anchor="end"
              >
                12 bytes
              </text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <!-- MOBILE STACK -->
          <div class="block md:hidden font-mono text-xs space-y-3">
            <div class="p-3 bg-[#FAF8F2] border-2 border-ink rounded">
              <div class="font-bold text-ink">
                <span class="text-[#C23000]">map&lt;string, uint64&gt;</span> counters = 1;
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="p-3 bg-[#FAF8F2] border-2 border-ink rounded font-bold text-ink">
              &#123;"a": 1, "b": 2&#125;
            </div>

            <div class="p-3 bg-[#FAF8F2] border-2 border-ink rounded space-y-2">
              <div class="font-bold text-[#C23000] uppercase">Protobuf</div>
              <div class="p-2.5 bg-white border border-ink/20 rounded text-[11px]">
                <div>message CountersEntry &#123; string key = 1; uint64 value = 2; &#125;</div>
                <div class="font-bold text-[#C23000]">repeated CountersEntry counters = 1;</div>
              </div>
              <div class="p-2.5 bg-white border border-ink/20 rounded text-sm font-bold leading-relaxed">
                <div>
                  <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">0A 05 0A</span> 01 61{' '}
                  <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">10</span> 01
                </div>
                <div>
                  <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">0A 05 0A</span> 01 62{' '}
                  <span class="text-[#FF4F18]">10</span> 02
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="text-right font-bold text-[#C23000]">14 bytes</div>
            </div>

            <div class="p-3 bg-ink text-paper border-2 border-ink rounded space-y-2">
              <div class="font-bold text-acid uppercase">OmniBuf</div>
              <div class="text-sm font-bold leading-relaxed">
                <div class="text-acid">3D 26 00 0A 00 05</div>
                <div>03 61 03</div>
                <div>03 62 05</div>
              </div>
              <div class="text-right font-bold text-acid">12 bytes</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
